---
// The apps one screen at a time, which platforms exist today, and Today in the terminal.
import Screenshot from "../Screenshot.astro";
import todayLight from "../../assets/screens/android-today-light.webp";
import todayDark from "../../assets/screens/android-today-dark.webp";
import boardLight from "../../assets/screens/android-board-light.webp";
import boardDark from "../../assets/screens/android-board-dark.webp";
import calendarLight from "../../assets/screens/android-calendar-light.webp";
import calendarDark from "../../assets/screens/android-calendar-dark.webp";

const phoneSizes = "(min-width: 60rem) 17rem, 72vw";
const phoneWidths = [300, 600, 900];
---

<section id="screens" aria-labelledby="screens-title">
  <h2 id="screens-title">One plan on every screen</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Your phone, your Mac, your Linux desktop and your terminal show the same plan. Each keeps its own copy, works
    offline and catches up when your server can be reached.
  </p>

  <div class="strip" role="region" aria-label="Screens of Dayhand for Android, scrolls sideways" tabindex="0">
    <figure class="shot">
      <Screenshot
        class="phone"
        light={todayLight}
        dark={todayDark}
        widths={phoneWidths}
        sizes={phoneSizes}
        alt="Today on Android: a summary card of the plan, the overdue invoices with a To today button, the task being worked on now with where it stopped, and the tasks for today with their times."
      />
      <figcaption><strong>Today.</strong> What is overdue, what you are on now and the rest of the day.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <Screenshot
        class="phone"
        light={boardLight}
        dark={boardDark}
        widths={phoneWidths}
        sizes={phoneSizes}
        alt="The board on Android with three tabs, To do 8, In progress 3 and Done 7. In progress shows the proposal for the bakery website marked Now, Update the pricing page at 16:00 and the case study for the logo project, each with its label."
      />
      <figcaption><strong>Board.</strong> To do, in progress and done, with labels and the task you are on now.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="shot">
      <Screenshot
        class="phone"
        light={calendarLight}
        dark={calendarDark}
        widths={phoneWidths}
        sizes={phoneSizes}
        alt="The week calendar on Android for 19 to 25 October 2026. Tasks sit at their times as blocks; the finished ones carry a check mark, and today's column is shaded."
      />
      <figcaption><strong>Calendar.</strong> A week and a day view, and a feed your calendar app can subscribe to.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <dl class="platforms">
    <div>
      <dt>Android</dt>
      <dd>Today, the week and day calendar, the board, repeats, checklists, reminders and approvals. Starts without any server.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>macOS</dt>
      <dd>Today, quick add from the menu bar or a global shortcut, reminders, the morning summary, the trash and each task's history.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Linux</dt>
      <dd>A Qt 6 app with Today, a quick add window for a key binding, a tray icon and desktop notifications. Follows Omarchy themes.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Terminal</dt>
      <dd><code>dayhand ui</code> shows Today, the board, the week and the trash full screen, with vim-style keys, in your terminal's colours.</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>iPhone and iPad <span class="badge wip">In the works</span></dt>
      <dd>Not out yet, so there is nothing to install or test. Until then the plan is on Android, macOS, Linux and the terminal.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <figure class="terminal">
    <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
    <pre tabindex="0" aria-label="The dayhand command printing Today"><code><span class="prompt">$</span> dayhand
<span class="out">Today, Sat 24 Oct 2026 (Europe/London)
NOW  #7 Write the proposal for the bakery website
     next: The pricing table is next
<span class="warn">OVERDUE (1)</span>
  #6   [ ]  yesterday  Send the October invoices                  #billing
TODAY
  #8   [ ]  09:30      Review the agent's pull request #18        #dev 1/3
  #9   [ ]  11:00      Call the accountant about VAT              #admin
  #11  [~]  16:00      Update the pricing page                    #site
  #12  [ ]  17:00      Publish the October newsletter             #marketing
  #7   [~]             Write the proposal for the bakery website  #clients now
  #13  [ ]             Back up the server                         #ops ↻
  #14  [ ]             Answer the support emails                  #support
  #20  [~]             Write the case study for the logo project  #marketing 2/3
DONE (1)
  #10  [x]  12:00      Export the Q3 sales report                 #billing</span></code></pre>
    <figcaption>The same plan in the terminal: <code>dayhand</code> alone prints Today.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="note">
    The apps and <code>dayhand ui</code> speak English, Polish, German, Spanish, French, Brazilian Portuguese, Japanese
    and Simplified Chinese.
  </p>
</section>
